    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\n2 1 3\n6\n1 2 3 1 2 3\n5\n3 2 3 2 1",
        "output": "1\n21\n11",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The only valid choice is the entire array. In detail:\n\nL=1,R=1L = 1, R = 1L=1,R=1: the resulting array is [3,1,3][3, 1, 3][3,1,3], which is missing 222.\nL=1,R=2L = 1, R = 2L=1,R=2: the resulting array is [3,2,3][3, 2, 3][3,2,3], which is missing 111.\nL=1,R=3L = 1, R = 3L=1,R=3: the resulting array is [3,2,1][3, 2, 1][3,2,1], which is good.\nL=2,R=2L = 2, R = 2L=2,R=2: the resulting array is [2,2,3][2, 2, 3][2,2,3], which is missing 111.\nL=2,R=3L = 2, R = 3L=2,R=3: the resulting array is [2,2,1][2, 2, 1][2,2,1], which is missing 333.\nL=3,R=3L = 3, R = 3L=3,R=3: the resulting array is [2,1,1][2, 1, 1][2,1,1], which is missing 333.\n\nTest case 222: Every subarray is a valid choice here.\nTest case 333: The valid subarrays (represented as pairs of (L,R)(L, R)(L,R)) are:\n(1,1),(1,2),(1,3),(1,5),(1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 5),(1,1),(1,2),(1,3),(1,5),\n(2,2),(2,3),(2,5),(2, 2), (2, 3), (2, 5),(2,2),(2,3),(2,5),\n(3,3),(3,4),(3,5),(3, 3), (3, 4), (3, 5),(3,3),(3,4),(3,5),\n(4,4)(4, 4)(4,4)"
      }
    ]
